              f"meridians twisted, dchi -> dchi + a(x), a on (t, S^3): to first order in a, the equation got by varying the twist, Ric(e_mu, n), is "
              f"(l/2) D^nu f_mu nu - 3 a_t/l along time and (l/2) D^nu f_i nu - 2 a_i/(l sin^2 chi) along the sphere, at three points "
              f"({_v39_r(e_h)}; the field part and the potential's part at the first point {_v39_f(rows_h[0][0], 6)} and {_v39_f(rows_h[0][1], 6)} "
              f"along time).  A constant potential a = 0.3 dt, with no field at all, gives {_v39_f(-3*0.3/l, 6)} = -3 a_t/l at chi = 0.5, 1.2 and "
